Recommends: open-iscsi, multipath-tools, sg3-utils, psmisc, lsscsi
Description: Synology NAS storage plugin for Proxmox VE (discovery stage)
 A Proxmox VE custom storage plugin for Synology NAS over iSCSI, in which one
 VM disk is one thin LUN on the NAS, so DSM's own snapshots and clones act on
 the unit an operator thinks about — no LVM layer and no shared LUN carved up
 locally.
 .
 THIS PACKAGE DOES NOT YET CONTAIN THE PLUGIN. Synology publishes no
 specification for the SAN Manager Web API, so the project is establishing the
 facts first. What ships here is pve-syno-api-probe, a read-only tool that asks
 a DSM what it actually supports and reports which questions remain open. It
 creates nothing and deletes nothing, and is safe to run against a production
 NAS.
 .
 Because the plugin itself is absent, this package does not depend on
 proxmox-ve: the probe is useful from any Debian host that can reach a DSM. The
 dependency will be added with the plugin.
